<%# Template text. Business details in [brackets] come from the STORE_* settings (config/store.js). Check the policy with a legal adviser. %>
<%- include('../partials/info-start', { heading: 'Privacy policy', lead: 'How we collect, use and protect your personal information when you shop with us.', updated: true }) %>
<article class="doc section-box" data-toc>
  <p>This policy explains how <%= store.legalName %> ("<%= store.brandName %>", "we", "us") handles your personal data when you use this website. By using the website you agree to this policy.</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, mobile number and password (stored only as a secure hash, never as plain text).</li>
    <li><strong>Delivery details:</strong> the addresses you save for delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Order and payment details:</strong> what you buy and the payment status. Card, UPI and bank details are entered on our payment partner's secure page. We never see or store your full card number or UPI PIN.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> anything you send us through the contact form or by email.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> a sign-in cookie that keeps you logged in, and basic server logs (such as IP address and browser type) used for security.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create and secure your account, and to process and deliver your orders.</li>
    <li>To reply to your questions and handle returns and refunds.</li>
    <li>To send order updates and, only if you subscribe, our newsletter. You can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
    <li>To prevent fraud and keep the website safe.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Sharing</h2>
  <p>We share only what is needed with our payment partner Razorpay to process payments, our delivery partners (couriers booked through Shiprocket) to ship your order, and authorities when the law requires it. We do not sell your personal data.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
  <p>We use one essential cookie to keep you signed in. Your wishlist, recently viewed items and light or dark theme choice are saved in your own browser (local storage) and stay on your device.</p>
  <p>If we turn on visitor analytics, a banner asks first. Only when you pick <strong>Allow analytics</strong> do we load it, to count visits and which products people look at. It is never used for ads, and your choice is kept in a cookie called <code>nx_consent</code> for 180 days. You can change it any time from <a href="/account/security#your-data">My Account, Login &amp; security</a>, and browsers that send Global Privacy Control are treated as a no.</p>
  <p>Signed in, you can download everything we keep about you as one file from the same page, or delete your account there.</p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>We keep account data while your account is open, and order records for as long as tax and accounting laws require (GST records, for example, are kept for 72 months after the annual return for that year is due).</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can view and update your profile and addresses from your account at any time. To ask for a copy of your data, or to close your account and delete your data, email <%= store.supportEmail %>.</p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>Passwords are hashed, the sign-in cookie cannot be read by scripts, and all traffic is encrypted over HTTPS. No system is perfectly secure, so please keep your password private.</p>

  <h2>8. Grievance officer</h2>
  <p>Under the Information Technology Act, 2000 and the rules made under it, you can contact our grievance officer:</p>
  <address class="doc-address">
    <%= store.grievanceOfficer %><br>
    <%= store.legalName %><br>
    <%= store.address %><br>
    Email: <%= store.supportEmail %>
  </address>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
</article>
<%- include('../partials/info-end', { scripts: ['doc-toc'] }) %>
